The default case returns nullptr, causing preclaim to return tecHAS_OBLIGATIONS.

`src/libxrpl/tx/transactors/account/AccountDelete.cpp:176-201`
```cpp
DeleterFuncPtr
nonObligationDeleter(LedgerEntryType t)
{
 switch (t)
 {
 case ltOFFER: return offerDelete;
 case ltSIGNER_LIST: return removeSignersFromLedger;
 case ltTICKET: return removeTicketFromLedger;
 case ltDEPOSIT_PREAUTH: return removeDepositPreauthFromLedger;
 case ltNFTOKEN_OFFER: return removeNFTokenOfferFromLedger;
 case ltDID: return removeDIDFromLedger;
 case ltORACLE: return removeOracleFromLedger;
 case ltCREDENTIAL: return removeCredentialFromLedger;
 case ltDELEGATE: return removeDelegateFromLedger;
 default: return nullptr; // ltSPONSORSHIP falls here!
 }
}
```

**Exploit scenario**: 1.

For transaction types with no granular permissions (like SignerListSet, AccountDelete), the sfDelegate field guarantees failure, but only at the checkPermission stage with a ter error.

`src/libxrpl/tx/Transactor.cpp:142-149`
```cpp
if (ctx.tx.isFieldPresent(sfDelegate))
{
 if (!ctx.rules.enabled(featurePermissionDelegationV1_1))
 return temDISABLED;
 if (ctx.tx[sfDelegate] == ctx.tx[sfAccount])
 return temBAD_SIGNER;
 // MISSING: check if tx type is delegable or has granular permissions
}
```

**Exploit scenario**: 1.

The ConfidentialMPTSend.h header also doesn't declare this override.

`src/libxrpl/tx/transactors/token/ConfidentialMPTSend.cpp:14-65`
```cpp
NotTEC
ConfidentialMPTSend::preflight(PreflightContext const& ctx)
{
 if (!ctx.rules.enabled(featureConfidentialTransfer))
 return temDISABLED;
 // ... no checkExtraFeatures override exists
 if (auto const err = credentials::checkFields(ctx.tx, ctx.j); !isTesSuccess(err))
 return err;
 return tesSUCCESS;
}
```

**Exploit scenario**: If featureConfidentialTransfer is activated before featureCredentials (unlikely but theoretically possible with independent amendment voting), an attacker could submit a ConfidentialMPTSend transaction with sfCredentialIDs that passes preflight validation (credentials::checkFields only checks format).

